  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two ideal batteries of emf <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and three resistances <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> are connected as shown in the figure. The current in resistance <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> would be zero if<br ><br/><img src=\"assets\\qt0011_c9f8039ad07c.png\"/></p>"
  },
